This is about Linguistics and Logic, this is written in French, and
this does not relate immediately to Lojban,

yet this is interesting, and I have the purpose to translate it in
English and to use it to exemplify some Lojban problematics

It says that

(1) predicates that are put together to build descriptions of an
object overlap (but we already knew that)

(2) given (1), it would be great to use some new kind of calculus in
which the "logical overlapping" property of things is granted by the
principles of the calculus

